I've been having pretty much fun changing NetHack 3.0j+ for my Macintosh.
Here are some super-simple fixes that will make the game *much* less
frustrating...

/* dogmove.c
   fn: dog_move(mtmp, after)
   around line 282 right after "ny = poss[i].y;" 

   This addendum keeps the dog from stepping right in front of you.
   I *hate* reading all those "you stop to avoid hitting..." messages. */

	if (u.umoved && (nx == (u.ux + u.dx) && ny == (u.uy + u.dy)))
		 goto nxti;	

/* hack.c
   fn: domove()
   around line 630 right after the "you chew through the..." code

   This addendum confirms drowns from walking into water.  Geeze I
   hate that.
*/

if(is_pool(x,y) && !(is_pool(u.ux,u.uy)))
	 if (!(Levitation 
#ifdef POLYSELF
	    || is_flyer(uasmon)
#endif
	    ))
		{
		pline("Step into the water? ");			
		if(yn() != 'y')
			{
			nomul(0);
			return;
			}
		}


OK. Enough of that.  Here are the fixes I'm playing with for myself. 
